  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nebraska received $1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Nebraska recorded 15,015 awards with an average award size of $66.8K, and obligations fell 20.7% year over year. Annual obligations have varied: FY21 $1.3B, FY22 $1.3B, FY23 $2B, FY24 $1.3B, FY25 $1.3B, and FY26 $1B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer so far with $360M, followed by the Department of Education with $287M and the General Services Administration with $169M. Other buying agencies in the top ten include the Department of Veterans Affairs, the Department of Agriculture, and the Department of State. The largest vendor by obligations is NELNET SERVICING LLC with $287M, followed by GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $154M. Other prominent vendors include HENDRICKSON TRANSPORTATION LLC and S365 INC. The top industries by obligations show a concentration in credit intermediation and IT services, with Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $287M and Computer Systems Design Services at $197M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 spending compare with recent years?",
        "body": "FY26 obligations are $1B, below the FY23 peak of $2B. Fiscal years FY21, FY22, FY24, and FY25 each recorded $1.3B, so FY26 is smaller than those years. Obligations fell 20.7% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drive federal buying in Nebraska?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $360M, followed by the Department of Education with $287M and the General Services Administration with $169M. Other top industries are Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $287M and Computer Systems Design Services at $197M. The vendor list mirrors those concentrations, with NELNET SERVICING LLC at $287M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $154M."
      }
    ]
  },
